# Testing

Read @.ai/rules/testing.md before adding or changing a test project, test package, or test. That file is the canonical testing standard.

- .NET tests use xUnit v3 on Microsoft.Testing.Platform. Do not add the VSTest stack, NUnit, MSTest, or TUnit.
- Test projects live under `tests/`, set `<OutputType>Exe</OutputType>`, reference `xunit.v3`, and are listed in `VppAggregator.slnx`.
- Versions are pinned only in the root `Directory.Packages.props`. A test project may reference only the approved test packages in that file. No mocking library and no assertion library. Use hand-written fakes and xUnit `Assert`.
- Module unit tests do not use Docker. Integration tests use `Testcontainers.PostgreSql` and the shared fixtures, not the compose stack.
- Pass `TestContext.Current.CancellationToken` into async calls. Wait on a `TaskCompletionSource` with `WaitAsync`. Do not use `Task.Delay` or `Thread.Sleep`.
- Database test conventions are in @.ai/rules/sql-ddl.md section 7. Python tests use pytest. Do not weaken `TestFrameworkTests`, skip hooks with `--no-verify`, or merge while `test-guardrail` is failing.
